{
 "id": "lem-coef-local-transport-section-colimits",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": null,
  "from": {
   "node": "prop-coef-integral-exceptional-adjoint",
   "place": "Proof paragraph 2, middle derived mapping-complex comparison before the inverse limit: Infinity-categorical monadicity and the augmented counit bar resolution. Supporting foundation: Free coherent monad modules and their augmented free resolution. Supporting lemma: Underlying equivalences and operadic colimits of coherent modules. Supporting step: Colimits of sections from preserved local fiber cocones.",
   "via": [
    "lem-coef-module-operadic-colimit-detection",
    "lem-coef-infinity-free-module-bar",
    "lem-coef-infinity-monadic-bar",
    "lem-coef-quillen-section-rectification",
    "lem-coef-semilinear-derived-sections",
    "lem-coef-finite-adjunction-diagram-realization"
   ]
  },
  "same_as": []
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Colimits of sections from preserved local fiber cocones",
 "statement": "Use the quasicategories, coherent functors, mapping spaces, colimits and universes of [def-cbc-enhanced-diagrams-cones], and inner and cocartesian fibrations of [def-coef-infinity-fibrations]. Let $q:E\\to S$ be a categorical fibration of quasicategories (an inner fibration lifting equivalence edges with prescribed source), assumed locally cocartesian, meaning that its pullback along each edge $\\Delta^1\\to S$ is a cocartesian fibration. For $s\\in S$ let $E_s$ be its fiber, and for $a:s\\to t$ let $a_!:E_s\\to E_t$ be local transport, determined by that edge pullback. Let $\\Gamma(q)=\\operatorname{Fun}_S(S,E)$ be the infinity-category of coherent sections, with transformations and higher simplices over the identity on $S$. All objects are small in a fixed sufficiently large universe.\n\nLet $K$ be a small simplicial set and $P:K\\to\\Gamma(q)$ a diagram. Suppose that for every $s\\in S$ its evaluation $P_s:K\\to E_s$ has a colimiting cocone $c_s:P_s\\to\\Delta_K l_s$, and that $a_!c_s$ is colimiting in $E_t$ for every edge $a:s\\to t$ of $S$. Then there exists a colimiting cocone $C:P\\to\\Delta_K L$ in $\\Gamma(q)$ whose evaluation at every $s$ is equivalent, as a cocone on $P_s$, to $c_s$. Under these hypotheses a cocone on $P$ is colimiting in $\\Gamma(q)$ if and only if all its evaluations are colimiting in the respective fibers. Only the specified fiber cocones and their local transports are assumed to be colimiting; no other colimits in the fibers or in $S$ are assumed, and $q$ need not be a globally cocartesian fibration.",
 "source": {
  "document": "https://people.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/HA.pdf",
  "place": "Higher Algebra (2017), dual of Lemma 3.2.2.9, printed pp. 362-363; combine with Higher Topos Theory (2009), Proposition 4.3.1.10 (locally cocartesian fiber criterion) and Proposition 4.3.1.5(4) (base change to the section fiber), printed pp. 262, 265-266. Online sources read; WANTED: archived Higher Algebra and Higher Topos Theory in literature/. No Stacks tag covers coherent section colimits."
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-cbc-enhanced-diagrams-cones",
  "def-coef-infinity-fibrations"
 ],
 "proof": [],
