n     \", \"doc\": \"Given a cocone $ c $ for a functor $ G : \\\\text{Grothendieck}(F) \\\\to \\\\mathcal{H} $, this constructs a cocone for the fiberwise colimit functor $ \\\\text{fiberwiseColimit} \\\\, G $. The apex of the new coco\"}\n  {\"name\": \"CategoryTheory.Limits.coconeOfCoconeFiberwiseColimit\", \"module\": \"Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Shapes/Grothendieck\", \"type\": \"{C : Type u₁} →\\n  [inst : CategoryTheory.Category.{v₁, u₁} C] →\\n    {F : CategoryTheory.Functor C CategoryTheory.Cat} →\\n      {H : Type u₂} →\\n        [inst_1 : CategoryTheory.Category.{v₂, u₂} H] →\\n          {G : CategoryTheory.Functor (CategoryTheory.Grothendieck F) H} →\\n            [inst_2 :\\n     \", \"doc\": \"Given a cocone $ c $ for the fiberwise colimit of a functor $ G : \\\\text{Grothendieck}(F) \\\\to \\\\mathcal{H} $, this constructs a cocone for $ G $ itself. The apex of the cocone is the same as $ c $'s ape\"}\n  {\"name\": \"CategoryTheory.Limits.coconeFiberwiseColimitOfCocone_ι_app\", \"module\": \"Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Shapes/Grothendieck\", \"type\": \"∀ {C : Type u₁} [inst : CategoryTheory.Category.{v₁, u₁} C] {F : CategoryTheory.Functor C CategoryTheory.Cat}\\n  {H : Type u₂} [inst_1 : CategoryTheory.Category.{v₂, u₂} H]\\n  {G : CategoryTheory.Functor (CategoryTheory.Grothendieck F) H}\\n  [inst_2 :\\n    ∀ {X Y : C} (f : X ⟶ Y),\\n      CategoryTheory.L\", \"doc\": \"For a cocone $ c $ over a functor $ G $ in the Grothendieck category of $ F : \\\\mathcal{C} \\\\to \\\\mathsf{Cat} $, the $ \\\\iota $-component of the fiberwise colimit cocone at an object $ X \\\\in \\\\mathcal{C} $\"}\n",
